<!-- Section 4.1 -->
<h2>4.1 Package Architecture Specification</h2>

<h3>4.1.2 Package Functions</h3>
<p>Table 4.1 shows the package functions for each architectural layer in the system.</p>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 35%;">Package</th>
            <th style="width: 65%;">Package Functions</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Layer</strong><br>(SDD_PKG_100)</td>
            <td>• To display form<br>• To display data and accept input data<br>• To update and validate input data<br>• To remove any data / submit requests</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Domain Layer (Controllers)</strong><br>(SDD_PKG_200)</td>
            <td>• To process system rules with logic<br>• To control the information from the view layer to the data access layer</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Data Access Layer (Eloquent Models)</strong><br>(SDD_PKG_300)</td>
            <td>• To establish and maintain the connection of database<br>• To keep the SQL statement<br>• To retrieve data from the database</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3>4.1.3 Package Content</h3>

<h4>View Layer (SDD_PKG_100)</h4>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 25%;">CLASS ID</th>
            <th style="width: 30%;">CLASS NAME</th>
            <th style="width: 45%;">FUNCTION</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
